Flagged: **Zone 3 is the outlier of the day** — wind sits at 96–100th percentile every hour *and* load hits the 100th percentile at hrs 9 and 12–15. Both drivers extreme simultaneously is rare and it carries the two highest-conviction names below.

Zone 4's shape matters more than its medians: wind is 12–14 GW at 96.8 pct overnight (hrs 1–8) then **collapses to 3.1–3.5 GW / 42–48 pct through hrs 14–18**, exactly when load peaks at 33.9 GW (hrs 16–17, 77–81 pct). So zone-4 wind-driven constraints are an overnight story and zone-4 load-driven constraints are an afternoon story — they do not overlap tomorrow. Zone 2 has the same collapse (100 pct at hr 1 → 35–51 pct hrs 15–20). Zones 5 and 21 have load down at 6.5–16 pct mid-afternoon.

