**Condition mismatch — DA is likely wrong here**

- **`xfmrsiouxcy-siouxcy`** — the clear one. It bound DA on `dt` (331) and your sheet records it as "high wind driven, wind: high". The Zone 1 lift says the opposite: **load +2.79, wind −0.78**. Tomorrow Zone 1 delivers high wind (83 on-peak / 93 off-peak) and only moderate load (62/72) — i.e. the driver the lift says *suppresses* it is elevated, and the driver that *drives* it is not. Both the DA print and your own sheet note point the same way, and the lift contradicts both. Name it explicitly and size down.
- **`xfmrsub1214-sub1214`** — bound DA on `dt` (110) with essentially **no lift in either direction** (load +0.22, wind −0.40), 1 trailing day, and Nov/Dec/Feb are its real months (26/28/24 days vs Aug 11). Fundamentals give no reason to expect it. The only argument for it is the four-element Sub-1209 outage stack opening tomorrow — which is an outage story, not a conditions story.
- **`xfmrcimarron-cimarron`** — softer case. Lift is Z2 load +1.37, and Z2 load is middling (59/75) with on-peak wind at only 54. Against that, **August is its single heaviest month (35 DA days)** and last year's window carried 7 DA days, plus the standing RIDGROTP–CIMARRON outage. Seasonality and outage say yes, conditions say unremarkable. Treat as neutral, not a mismatch.

