## 6. Gaps

1. **`linked_outages` is empty for all 20 constraints** — the join under-reports. Morrison–Sooner and Mustang–SW 5th are both clearly on-path and both missing from it. I reconstructed causality from `sched_outages` instead.
2. **Ten of the 20 constraints were scored against Zone 4 by default**, not by operator choice — the sheet has no `reserve_zone` for them. Six of those ten are geographically wrong: `lneastruth-minot_rev23` and `lnpenn_tap-devilsl` (North Dakota), `xfmrmcleodn-mcleodn` (Minnesota), `lntoyne_cb-carlntcb` and `lnlime_ck-bartonss_rev23` (Iowa), `xfmrsub1214-sub1214` (Nebraska). **Their lift numbers are computed against Oklahoma/Kansas fundamentals and should not be trusted.** The other four defaults (`lnsw51-6`, `lnmdwst-frnkln1`, `lnbois_tap`, `lnwr_smkhl-summ`) are plausibly zone 4 on geography. Assigning reserve zones to the six would materially change their reads.
3. **Five constraints returned "could not find the dfax value"** — no node picks at all: `lnlime_ck-bartonss_rev23` (the day's largest), `lnsw51-6_me4_rev23`, `lnbois_tap-commtap4_rev23`, `lneastruth-minot_rev23`, `lnpenn_tap-devilsl`, `xfmrsub1214-sub1214`. Note this hits the two best-explained new constraints, so there is no way to express them at a node from this run.
4. **`lnmdwst-frnkln1` has a dfax table but n=0 on every one of its 59 nodes** — no price history, so no metrics.
5. **Record depth is conditioned on today's constraint numbers, not on the monitored line.** `lnmdwst-frnkln1` shows 1 binding day in 104 weeks for constraint 401270 while the sheet holds 9 prior rows for that name — those rows are almost certainly other contingencies on the same line. So "first bind ever" means first bind *for this monitored/contingency pair*. Same caveat applies to the other `_rev23` names.
6. **RT history is structurally absent for many DA-heavy names** — `lnrussett-sbrown` (552 DA / 0 RT days), `lnvinetap3-nhays` (245/0), `xfmrcimarron-cimarron` (242/0), `lnmonett-aur1241` (139/0). No RT-active day in two years, so these appear to be DA-enforced only. Not a fetch error, but it means no RT cross-check is available for them.
7. `predict_tomorrow_percentile` returned data for all six zones (1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 21) — **no missing forecast dates**. No constraint raised an exception; all 20 completed.

Sheet untouched — read-only, as specified. Logs at `QCTest/Manual_bidding/logs/scratch/run.log` and `history.log`.

